{"kind":"artifact","text":"The committed embed, rebuilt from the browser source carrying the signing-boundary dispatcher. Exact clean pushed head 6bcb4798e07efe3a8c8de4a495e709520cf099e7 on request/planner-dr-recut; checkout clean, local and origin identical. Successor to 95597ffc at this path.\n\nTHIS PATH IS WHERE MY OWN DEFECT SHOWED, so it is worth recording plainly rather than presenting a clean result. I committed the ui/src changes for the signing guards without rebuilding the embed. make ui-check then failed and make ui left three files dirty: the old bundle deleted, index.html modified, a new bundle untracked. The committed embed did not match what the source produced, which means the resident would have served a browser nobody had reviewed at this head.\n\nThe gate caught it, which is what it is for. I did not paper over it with a third commit that regenerated the embed after the fact, because that would have left the first commit's own head failing its own gate — a head that cannot pass its gate is not a reviewable head, even when the tip of the branch passes. Instead I rebuilt both commits so the embed sits in the same commit as the source change that caused it. The branch was unpushed past 97a749ec, so no hash anyone had seen moved.\n\nVERIFIED AFTER THE REBUILD, not assumed: make ui exits 0 and leaves git status completely empty, so the committed bundle is byte-identical to what the current ui/src produces; make ui-check exits 0. Both were re-run at this exact head after the final commit, not at an intermediate one.","body":{"commit":"6bcb4798e07efe3a8c8de4a495e709520cf099e7","path":"internal/service/uidist"}}